# The shapes of node the compiler names (decision node-refinements): each a named pattern of a case of node.warp, so
# `d: Definition` holds one, `n is Definition` tests it and the arm `Definition: …` takes it apart into its names.
# A shape gets a name once several functions take it; the cases themselves (Key, List, Symbol …) are types already.
pattern Pair = Key(key, Op.Colon, value)
pattern Definition = Key(head, Op.Define, body)
pattern Member = Key(owner, Op.Dot, field)
pattern Block = List(statements, Bracket.Curly, separator)
